WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.834
-Thank you so much for being on
the show. I appreciate it.

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:04.067
-Dude, I've wanted to be here
forever, man.

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:05.501
Thanks for finally having me.

00:00:05.501 --> 00:00:06.868
-Oh, my God. Come on.

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:08.701
I want to talk about
your film "Devotion."

00:00:08.701 --> 00:00:12.534
But first I got to say, congrats
on "Top Gun: Maverick."

00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:14.767
What a great job you did
in that film.

00:00:14.767 --> 00:00:16.767
-Thank you, thank you.
-You were amazing.

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:18.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
I was like, you're crushing it.

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:21.934
I watched it on the IMAX.
It was so fun.

00:00:21.934 --> 00:00:25.200
You just popped off the screen.
But then the movie went on

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.033
to make over a billion dollars,
by the way.

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:30.734
-A billion. It's not bad.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:30.734 --> 00:00:33.934
-How does it feel to be
in such a giant movie?

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:37.234
-I mean, it's incredible.
It's definitely changed my life.

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:41.100
I'm feeling grateful
for every moment.

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.701
I still feel like people don't
know my name.

00:00:42.701 --> 00:00:44.901
Everybody calls me Hangman,
still, which is great.

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:49.901
I did get to do a really cool
thing with Jerry Bruckheimer.

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:53.167
Jerry Bruckheimer, who is
the producer of "Top Gun."

00:00:53.167 --> 00:00:55.334
-Legendary.
-He threw a billion-dollar party

00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:56.868
at his house --
didn't cost a billion dollars.

00:00:56.868 --> 00:00:59.667
It's because we crossed
a billion dollars.

00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:03.000
But he threw a billion-dollar
party at his house.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.501
-You got to feel like --

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:06.100
You go, "That's it. I'm on top
of the world."

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.167
-Yeah, I mean, it was like --

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:08.467
He had the Porsche
from the movie.

00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:10.234
He had the motorcycle
from the movie.

00:01:10.234 --> 00:01:13.434
All the cast was there.
We're just all hanging out.

00:01:13.434 --> 00:01:15.667
We're playing trivia games,
having the best time.

00:01:15.667 --> 00:01:20.667
And I feel like because I seem
like a guy who loves karaoke --

00:01:20.667 --> 00:01:22.901
[ Laughter ]
-You seem like a guy?

00:01:22.901 --> 00:01:24.267
-I feel like I'm a guy
that you're like,

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:26.334
"Oh, he has one drink
and wants to do karaoke."

00:01:26.334 --> 00:01:28.300
I'm not that guy.
-Wow!

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.200
-Yeah, I just feel like I give
off that vibe.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:33.234
-Yeah, you got a karaoke vibe.
-Yeah, I'm like the guy

00:01:33.234 --> 00:01:35.467
who's like, "Okay, he'll grab
a drink with me."

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:36.868
-"We'll do a song, yeah."

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:38.701
-"He's not going to be good, but
he's going to have a good time."

00:01:38.701 --> 00:01:41.367
I actually hate karaoke.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:44.801
But Jerry, at this party,

00:01:44.801 --> 00:01:48.334
he teamed everybody up
to do karaoke.

00:01:48.334 --> 00:01:50.767
And my song was
"Take My Breath Away"...

00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:52.601
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.601 --> 00:01:55.901
...which is, like, just not
in my octave range at all.

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:57.801
-No, it's hard to be
in anyone's -- Yeah.

00:01:57.801 --> 00:01:59.634
That's a really tricky song.

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:02.200
-And so Danny Ramirez,
who plays Fanboy in the movie,

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.501
we were paired up to sing
that song.

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:08.934
And I sang it. And I go,
"Hey, dude, we just got to

00:02:08.934 --> 00:02:10.300
fully commit to this thing.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:12.367
If we're going to do this,
we got to fully commit."

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:15.834
But I think we kind of,
like, overcommitted.

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:18.033
And we went, like --

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:20.968
We basically were, like, rolling
around on couches and, like --

00:02:20.968 --> 00:02:23.567
-Trying to sell it.
-Rubbing centerpieces

00:02:23.567 --> 00:02:25.567
on each other and we were like
behind curtains.

00:02:25.567 --> 00:02:27.767
-Whatever you can do
to get some type of reaction.

00:02:27.767 --> 00:02:30.701
-Yeah. And it was just like,
everybody was just stone-faced.

00:02:30.701 --> 00:02:33.767
And it was like the most
powerful people in Hollywood,

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:35.667
everybody that I love
and respect.

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:38.267
-"Why am I doing this?"
-I just lost all respect

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:41.501
from them in a matter of
3 1/2 minutes of this song.

00:02:41.501 --> 00:02:44.701
-You did do some -- You do some
cool things, by the way.

00:02:44.701 --> 00:02:46.801
Because I did hear about this.
Is this true?

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:49.868
Tom Cruise gifted you
pilot lessons?

00:02:49.868 --> 00:02:52.133
-Yeah. I'm a fully licensed
pilot now. Yeah.

00:02:52.133 --> 00:02:54.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:57.901
-Tom has been on the show
a zillion times.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:03:01.133
He's never gifted me
pilot lessons ever.

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:02.667
-You probably did something
wrong.

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:04.501
I don't know.
-I did, yeah.

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:06.200
Did he know were you
into flying?

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:09.200
-Yeah. I mean, while we were
shooting "Top Gun,"

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:11.000
we flew in all
these different airplanes.

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.801
And I just, you know, had
a real love for aviation.

00:03:13.801 --> 00:03:19.634
So for Christmas, he gave me my
pilot's lessons, flying lessons.

00:03:19.634 --> 00:03:22.367
So, as I was flying and getting
that license, I'd send him

00:03:22.367 --> 00:03:25.167
pictures of all the different
stuff I was flying in.

00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:26.934
So I was finally in
my last check ride.

00:03:26.934 --> 00:03:31.133
I get on the ground and get back
to the hangar, and on the table

00:03:31.133 --> 00:03:34.167
is a note from Tom that said,
"Welcome to the skies."

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:37.067
And it was a certificate
for stunt driving lessons.

00:03:37.067 --> 00:03:39.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.234 --> 00:03:41.534
-You don't stop.
Tom Cruise doesn't stop.

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:44.467
He goes to the next level.

00:03:44.467 --> 00:03:45.901
-He's gotten me into skydiving.

00:03:45.901 --> 00:03:47.634
He's gotten me into
motorcycle riding.

00:03:47.634 --> 00:03:50.133
The guy is just, you know,
he convinces you to do

00:03:50.133 --> 00:03:51.934
all the most dangerous things
on this planet.

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:54.133
-He made you --
He didn't make you,

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:57.234
but he also gave you
a gift of skydiving?

00:03:57.234 --> 00:03:59.434
-Yeah, that was actually --

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:01.801
It was actually my second date
with my girlfriend,

00:04:01.801 --> 00:04:03.634
which it's actually our
anniversary tomorrow,

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:05.467
so happy anniversary.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:05.467 --> 00:04:06.667
-Congratulations.
-Yeah.

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.501
-No, but tell everyone
what happens.

00:04:08.501 --> 00:04:09.834
Because when Tom Cruise
just goes,

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:11.300
"Oh, let's go skydiving"
or whatever,

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:12.601
here's what he does.

00:04:12.601 --> 00:04:16.234
Tell everyone.
-So, basically, I go,

00:04:16.234 --> 00:04:20.267
"Hey, Tom" -- We were going to
go do some reshoots in London.

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:22.701
And I said, "Hey, man, I want to
go skydiving while I'm out here.

00:04:22.701 --> 00:04:25.200
I hear the skydiving is great."
He goes, "Yeah."

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.601
And he sends a helicopter
for me.

00:04:26.601 --> 00:04:29.834
But it got so windy that
the skydiving team --

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:31.501
I was with the U.K. skydiving
team -- they said

00:04:31.501 --> 00:04:34.067
it's so dangerous, we should not
go skydiving.

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:37.100
I was like, "Alright.
I'm no hero. I'm good."

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:38.901
-I don't have to hear that
twice. We're good.

00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:41.567
-So, we scrapped it, went back.

00:04:41.567 --> 00:04:44.000
And then Tom hit me up like a
couple weeks later and was like,

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.567
"Hey, man, what are you,
scared?"

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:47.100
And I'm like, "What are you
talking about?"

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.334
And he's like, "You never took
me up on the skydiving."

00:04:49.334 --> 00:04:51.667
I'm like, "Oh, I'll do it
whenever, man."

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:54.901
So, with the girl that I was
seeing at the time,

00:04:54.901 --> 00:04:57.534
this is our second date,
we went skydiving.

00:04:57.534 --> 00:05:02.701
And when I got there, Tom --
I found out that Tom's

00:05:02.701 --> 00:05:04.400
only request is that Glen

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:06.868
cannot go skydiving
with another person.

00:05:06.868 --> 00:05:09.901
He has to go solo
the first time.

00:05:09.901 --> 00:05:16.434
So I literally have to jump out
of this plane by myself.

00:05:16.434 --> 00:05:18.667
But the worst part is that

00:05:18.667 --> 00:05:21.501
I couldn't find my tab
when I was falling.

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:22.701
-This is the nightmare that --

00:05:22.701 --> 00:05:24.267
-It's the nightmare that
everybody talks about.

00:05:24.267 --> 00:05:27.367
But my first thought, which is
not like a selfless thought,

00:05:27.367 --> 00:05:31.601
but my first thought was,
"Oh, Tom just killed me.

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:34.100
He's going to feel so bad."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.601
-You're thinking about
Tom's feelings?

00:05:36.601 --> 00:05:38.801
-I was like, "God, he pushed me
to do this thing."

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:40.534
-Yeah, it's really gonna hurt
his feelings.

00:05:40.534 --> 00:05:43.300
-I'm looking for the tab and I'm
like, "You're not Tom Cruise.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.868
You'll never be Tom Cruise.
Why did you do this?"

00:05:45.868 --> 00:05:47.734
-And then you pulled the thing.
-And then I finally pulled it.

00:05:47.734 --> 00:05:49.400
I was way below altitude.
-You were Tom Cruise.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:50.634
-Came in hot.
-Yeah.

00:05:50.634 --> 00:05:52.767
-Made it, went back up,
did it again.

00:05:52.767 --> 00:05:54.033
-You did it twice?
-Yeah, twice.

00:05:54.033 --> 00:05:56.067
-That's Glen Powell. That's what
I'm talking about there.

00:05:56.067 --> 00:05:57.267
That's how you do it.

00:05:57.267 --> 00:05:58.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:58.701 --> 00:06:00.868
That's how you do it, bud.

00:06:00.868 --> 00:06:03.033
Let's talk about your new film,
"Devotion."

00:06:03.033 --> 00:06:05.067
You're getting great reviews
on this.

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:07.067
It's based on a true story.

00:06:07.067 --> 00:06:08.701
How did you get involved
with this?

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:12.400
-This is a project I've been
developing for five years.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.634
It's a project that's so close
to my heart.

00:06:14.634 --> 00:06:16.033
I love this movie so much.

00:06:16.033 --> 00:06:19.934
It's about the most famous
aviator duo in naval history,

00:06:19.934 --> 00:06:22.701
first African-American naval
aviator and his wingman.

00:06:22.701 --> 00:06:25.634
They pulled all sorts of daring
missions behind enemy lines.

00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:28.567
Not to spoil anything,
but one of them gets shot down

00:06:28.567 --> 00:06:31.033
behind enemy lines and the other
one crash-lands his plane

00:06:31.033 --> 00:06:32.467
on purpose to save him.

00:06:32.467 --> 00:06:34.300
Just this beautiful story
of how far

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.000
you're willing to go
for a wingman.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.100
Please see it.
It's coming out on Thanksgiving.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.601
And I just --
Take the whole family.

00:06:39.601 --> 00:06:40.901
It's just awesome.

00:06:40.901 --> 00:06:44.467
But yeah, it's just this project
that's just been my baby,

00:06:44.467 --> 00:06:46.934
and I had to go meet
the families to get the rights

00:06:46.934 --> 00:06:50.400
and put this thing together.
-They gave you the thumbs-up?

00:06:50.400 --> 00:06:54.300
-Yeah. It was sort of like
I guess like asking for

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.033
a girl's permission to marry.

00:06:56.033 --> 00:06:58.467
You know, it kind of felt like
you're asking, you know,

00:06:58.467 --> 00:07:00.701
you're asking the family
to tell their story.

00:07:00.701 --> 00:07:03.734
And I sat down with Tom Hudner,
the guy I'm playing in the movie

00:07:03.734 --> 00:07:05.701
and I remember saying, you know,

00:07:05.701 --> 00:07:07.100
it was after
a three-day weekend.

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:08.400
I thought it was
just going great.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.133
We were having,
like, a great time,

00:07:10.133 --> 00:07:12.534
and I was asking him about his
experience in the Korean War.

00:07:12.534 --> 00:07:13.968
-Then he's like, "Do you want to
do karaoke?"

00:07:13.968 --> 00:07:15.367
-He's like, "You want to do
karaoke?"

00:07:15.367 --> 00:07:16.801
and I was like, "Oh, no!"

00:07:16.801 --> 00:07:19.200
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:22.367
And I was like, you know, "I'd
love to play you in the movie."

00:07:22.367 --> 00:07:24.601
And it was just
like dead silent.

00:07:24.601 --> 00:07:27.934
And I was like, "Okay, I thought
this was going a little better."

00:07:27.934 --> 00:07:30.534
I guess it's better for me
than it was for you.

00:07:30.534 --> 00:07:34.634
And then he left, came back with
a signed photo of him

00:07:34.634 --> 00:07:37.601
getting the Medal of Honor, and
he said, "Just get it right."

00:07:37.601 --> 00:07:38.968
-Yeah.

00:07:38.968 --> 00:07:41.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
Just get it right, buddy.

00:07:41.133 --> 00:07:42.767
You got it right.
You got it right.

00:07:42.767 --> 00:07:43.968
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:43.968 --> 00:07:45.834
Here's Glen Powell
in "Devotion."

00:07:45.834 --> 00:07:47.501
Take a look at this.

00:07:47.501 --> 00:07:50.834
-I'm sticking my neck out
for you.

00:07:50.834 --> 00:07:54.734
-Sticking your neck out
with a piece of paper?

00:07:56.701 --> 00:07:57.934
Tom.

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:03.167
That paper cost you nothing.

00:08:03.167 --> 00:08:05.067
Nothing!

00:08:05.067 --> 00:08:08.801
You know how tired I am of
people trying to help me

00:08:08.801 --> 00:08:10.567
while looking down on me?

00:08:13.534 --> 00:08:15.434
-I am not looking down on you.

00:08:19.434 --> 00:08:21.033
What do you want me to do?

00:08:26.634 --> 00:08:28.334
-Just be my wingman.

00:08:29.367 --> 00:08:30.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:30.667 --> 00:08:32.334
-Glen Powell, everybody.

00:08:32.334 --> 00:08:35.300
"Devotion" opens in theaters
November 23rd.

